  "notes": [
   "The parts are the same as in step 1, with no additions or removals.",
   "The schematic shows one end of the potentiometer on 5V, the other end on GND, and the wiper on A0. I placed the potentiometer on a breadboard in one row (columns 10, 11 and 12, row a) and used three jumper wires to the Uno, because the tutorial's circuit image didn't load.",
   "The potentiometer's end legs are interchangeable, so which end goes to 5V and which to GND is arbitrary. I put 5V on VCC and GND on GND.",
   "The LED is the Uno's built-in LED on pin 13, so there is no external LED or resistor and no wire to pin 13."
  ]
